Subject: Fetch nodes separately so kubectl admit reserves cluster node cost

Why: Upstream combines cluster-scoped Kueue CRDs and `nodes` into one comma-joined `kubectl get <crds>,nodes -o json` call. Because Kueue CRDs are not in `deploy/sandbox/kubectl-admit.py`'s `KINDS` table, `scope_of()` (`all(k in clustered for k in kinds)`) classifies the combined command as `NAMESPACE_SCOPE` (`charged=False`) and skips the 255 MiB `fleet`-tier memory reservation for `get nodes cluster json`. Fetching `nodes` in its own `kubectl get nodes -o json` call lets `kubectl-admit` reserve its profiled memory cost cleanly.
Local-Issue: none (adoption of gke-kueue-troubleshooting from google/skills)
Eval-Case: kueue-troubleshooting-mixed-flavor-tas-probe
Upstream-Issue: none (specific to this repository)
Retire-When: `deploy/sandbox/kubectl-admit.py` charges mixed-kind queries containing any cluster-scoped kind or upstream fetches `nodes` separately

